+# Glossary
+
+**Billing period** — half-open `[period_start, period_end)`; the renewal is billed on
+`period_end`. During a trial the current period is the free trial.
+
+**Upgrade** — a plan change to a plan with a higher *monthly* list price, whatever the interval.
+Applies immediately with proration. See ADR 0001.
+
+**Downgrade** — a plan change to a plan with a lower monthly list price. Scheduled for the
+period end; nothing billed or credited at the request.
+
+**Interval switch** — changing between monthly and annual billing. Scheduled for the period
+end; never refunds unused time.
+
+**Scheduled change** — the one pending plan/interval target a subscription moves to at its next
+renewal (`Subscription.scheduled_change`). Replaced by each new request.
+
+**Proration** — billing part of a period: `price × remaining days / days in period`, rounded
+half-up to cents per line. Remaining days count from the change date (inclusive) to the period
+end (exclusive).
+
+**Credit line** — negative line on an upgrade invoice for the unused part of the current plan.
