@@ -0,0 +1,112 @@
+# Mid-cycle plan changes
+
+## What and why
+
+Customers cannot change plan today: support cancels and resubscribes them by hand. Add
+mid-cycle plan changes: upgrades and downgrades, optionally switching between monthly and
+annual billing, prorated so nobody pays twice for the same days.
+
+## Interface (fixed — copied verbatim)
+
+- `BillingService.change_plan(subscription_id: str, new_plan_code: str, new_interval: Interval | None = None) -> Invoice | None`
+  in `src/billing/service.py`. `new_interval=None` keeps the subscription's current interval.
+- Return the invoice issued for the change (recorded in the store like every other invoice),
+  or `None` when nothing is billed at the moment of the request.
+- Add `InvalidPlanChange(BillingError)` to `src/billing/errors.py` for change requests that
+  can't be honoured; keep using the existing error classes where they already fit.
+
+## Rules
+
+The *target* of a request is `(new_plan_code, new_interval or current interval)`.
+
+**Classification** — by comparing the two plans' **monthly** list prices only, whatever the
+interval: more expensive = upgrade, cheaper = downgrade. Same plan with another interval is an
+interval switch (neither).
+
+**Active subscription**
+- *Upgrade*: applies now. `plan_code` changes, `period_start`/`period_end` do not. One invoice,
+  issued on the change date, with exactly two lines, both at the prices of the **current**
+  interval:
+  1. credit `-(old price × remaining / period days)` for the unused part of the current plan;
+  2. charge `+(new price × remaining / period days)` for the same days on the new plan.
+
+  `remaining` = days from the change date (inclusive) to `period_end` (exclusive); `period days`
+  = `period_end - period_start`. Each line is computed exactly and rounded half-up to cents on
+  its own; the total is the sum of the two rounded lines. The next renewal bills the new plan at
+  full price.
+- *Upgrade with an interval switch*: split. The upgrade applies now as above; the interval
+  switch is scheduled for the period end.
+- *Downgrade* and *interval switch*: scheduled for the period end. Returns `None`; nothing is
+  billed, refunded or credited. The renewal moves the subscription to the target plan and
+  interval, starts a period of that interval and bills its full price.
+
+**Scheduled change**
+- At most one per subscription. Each request states its full target and replaces whatever was
+  scheduled.
+- An upgrade that applies now discards anything scheduled, unless the same request schedules
+  an interval switch (which then replaces it).
+- A scheduled change has not happened: an upgrade while a downgrade is pending is prorated from
+  the current plan.
+- Requesting the current plan and interval cancels the scheduled change and returns `None`; if
+  nothing is scheduled it raises `InvalidPlanChange`.
+
+**Free trial**: any change (upgrade, downgrade, interval) applies immediately in full. No
+proration, no invoice, returns `None`, trial end unchanged. Trial end bills the full price of the
+plan and interval in force then.
+
+**Rejections** (a rejected request records no invoice and leaves the subscription untouched):
+- unknown subscription → `SubscriptionNotFound`
+- canceled subscription → `SubscriptionNotActive`
+- unknown target plan → `PlanNotFound`
+- retired target plan → `PlanNotAvailable` (leaving a retired plan is allowed)
+- current plan and interval with nothing scheduled → `InvalidPlanChange`
+
+**Implementer's decisions** (the user had no view; recorded in ADR 0001):
+- Different plan with the *same* monthly price: not an upgrade → scheduled for the period end.
+- Interval-only switch while staying on a retired plan → `PlanNotAvailable` (it is a new sale of
+  a retired plan). Cancelling a scheduled change by requesting a retired current plan is allowed.
+- Request on or after `period_end` before the renewal job has run → `InvalidPlanChange`.
+- A scheduled change whose target plan is retired afterwards still applies at renewal.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- [ ] Pro (30/mo) → Premium (75/mo) on Mar 11 in a Mar 1–Apr 1 period returns an invoice dated
+      Mar 11 with lines `-20.32`, `+50.81`, total `30.49`, recorded in the store; the
+      subscription is on Premium with the same period.
+- [ ] The renewal after an upgrade bills the new plan's full price for a period of the same
+      interval.
+- [ ] An upgrade on an annual subscription is prorated at annual prices.
+- [ ] An upgrade on the first day of the period credits and charges the full period prices.
+- [ ] Each line is rounded half-up on its own (the example's total is 30.49, not 30.48).
+- [ ] A downgrade returns `None`, records no invoice, leaves plan and period unchanged; the
+      renewal bills the cheaper plan's full price.
+- [ ] Monthly → annual and annual → monthly on the same plan return `None`, record no invoice;
+      the renewal starts a period of the new interval and bills its full price.
+- [ ] Upgrade + interval switch: invoice prorated at the current interval's prices, interval
+      unchanged now; the renewal is the new plan on the new interval at full price.
+- [ ] A second request replaces the scheduled change.
+- [ ] An upgrade while a downgrade is pending is prorated from the current plan and discards
+      the downgrade.
+- [ ] An upgrade with an interval switch while a downgrade is pending replaces the downgrade
+      with the interval switch.
+- [ ] Requesting the current plan and interval cancels a scheduled change (`None`); with nothing
+      scheduled it raises `InvalidPlanChange`.
+- [ ] During a trial, upgrade, downgrade and interval change apply immediately, return `None`,
+      record no invoice, keep the trial end; trial end bills the new plan/interval in full.
+- [ ] Each rejection raises the listed error, records no invoice and leaves the subscription
+      unchanged.
+- [ ] A customer on a retired plan can change to an active plan.
+- [ ] The implementer's decisions above each have a test.
+- [ ] `python3 -m pytest -q` exits 0.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- Account credit balances, refunds, negative invoices for downgrades.
+- Customer-specific or discounted prices: credits use the current plan's list price.
+- Moving the billing date (anchor) of a period.
+- Changing a canceled subscription back to life.
+
+## Scope limits
+
+`src/billing/` (service, subscriptions, errors, money, `__init__`), tests, README, this spec,
+`docs/adr/0001-plan-change-timing.md`, `GLOSSARY.md`. No new dependencies; no store API change.
